# resize-transient-e2e — looprs-zie
# measured 2026-10-08, aarch64-apple-darwin (Apple Silicon), macOS
#
# commands:
#   cargo build && python3 spikes/resize_transient_e2e.py
#   LOOPRS_BIN=/tmp/looprs-prefix python3 spikes/resize_transient_e2e.py
#
# The pre-ticket control binary is `96e745c` (looprs-6cj), built and copied to
# /tmp/looprs-prefix before restoring this ticket's src/.
#
# A 400,000-line short-line flood through the real app in a real pty, then a
# 16-step window drag across 30..100 columns with RSS sampled every 20 ms.
# Both builds: app alive, drag survived, RSS flat. RSS cannot resolve the
# per-frame transient (freed memory stays resident) and the shipped 256 KiB
# per-view transcript buffer keeps this scenario well clear of the pathological
# sizing; see spikes/results/resize-transient.log for the in-process numbers
# that do.

